# VFX-12 per-placement User Parameters (UE UNiagaraComponent::OverrideParameters): two placements of one system,
# Content/VFX/Demo/Impact.dfx (the engine Impact template made a looping demo: system Loop, emitters Infinite every
# 1.5 s, so the burst repeats in the editor viewport without Play), each with its own SurfaceNormal override.
# Scene Content/Scenes/VFX_Demo_Impacts.desce: ImpactUp at x=-150 (SurfaceNormal 0,1,0), ImpactPlusX at x=+150
# (SurfaceNormal 1,0,0). The edit goes through the Details write path (`set <entity> <Type>.<Field>`: the same
# reflected write, undo record and dirty scene as a hand edit); the User Parameters section then shows the row.
# The scenario dirties the scene but does not save it.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/VFX_Demo_Impacts.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,30,320
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,0,-1
Дано run Panel "Open Particle Debugger"
# Simulate starts the effects from age zero (Scene::SetState resets the VFXWorld, as UE's fresh SIE world); the
# effects are frozen first so the shot is a chosen fixed step (6 x 1/60 s = 0.1 s), not wherever the clock lands.
Дано run Debug "Particles: Freeze"
Когда run Action Simulate
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда state
Тогда-вид 1a_flipbook_early two steps in (1/30 s, early in the flash's 0.14-0.22 s life): each flash is the first cell of T_ImpactFlash - a broad glowing star with long thin rays (Kenney star_09), not a round blurred disc; the sparks are thin straight streaks (trace_01)
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда state
Тогда 0_debugger the Particle Debugger (frozen) lists Dust, Flash and Sparks of both ImpactUp and ImpactPlusX with Total spawned > 0 and Alive > 0 for Flash and Sparks
Когда state
Тогда-вид 1_impacts each impact shows a flash whose shape is a later cell of the T_ImpactFlash flipbook (a thinner four-ray star, different from 1a_flipbook_early) and velocity-aligned spark streaks textured from T_ImpactSpark; the left one (x=-150) throws them upward, the right one (x=+150) sideways along +X - the difference is plain to the eye
Когда run Action Stop
Когда run Entity "Add to selection ImpactPlusX"
Когда set selected VFX.Overrides[0].Value 0,0,1,0
# A chosen moment, not wherever the editor clock lands: the effects restart from age zero and step 0.1 s, frozen.
Когда run Debug "Particles: Freeze"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Restart"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда run Debug "Particles: Step"
Когда state
Тогда 2_details Details of ImpactPlusX shows the "User Parameters" section with a ticked (overridden) Vec3 row SurfaceNormal = 0, 0, 1; in the viewport frozen 0.1 s after a restart, the right burst throws toward the camera (+Z, a round splash seen whole) while the left one still throws upward
